# The Silver Ford: a wide black river, Old Bram and his dark ferry, and
# on an island in the middle, the Lady's shrine glowing blue.

place the ford
  title: The Silver Ford
  the sky: night
  the mist: light
  the ground: pebbles, 50 by 44 m
  you come in at 10 18, facing -30

  a river at 0 -8
  a broken bridge at -8 -8, turned 90
  a ferry boat at 4 -1.6, turned 90
  a ferry lantern at 1.8 0.6, unlit
  Old Bram at 3 2.2, facing 160
  a shrine called the far shrine at 3 -19

  a way to the woods at 14 20, turned 140
  a way to the peak at -20 6, turned 90

  20 reeds in a line from -24 -1.8 to 24 -1.8
  12 reeds between -22 -2.5 and 22 -1
  12 rocks between -22 1 and 22 20
  10 pine trees between -24 6 and 24 21
  6 tall pines between -24 -15 and 24 -21

  when you first arrive
    say: The woods open onto the river. It's wide and fast and black, and the moon lies on it in broken pieces.
    say: Out in the middle, on a little island, something glows blue.

  when you talk to Old Bram
    if bram will row
      Old Bram: In you get. Mind the oar.
      go to the island
    otherwise
      Old Bram: Ferry's closed. Lantern's out. Nobody crosses the Silver Ford in the dark. Not since my grandmother's time.
      choose
        choice if you have the honey bread: I have honey bread. Would you row me across for it?
          say: Bram sniffs the cloth. His whole face changes.
          Old Bram: Is that Hesta's? I haven't eaten since the lamps went out. Fine. Fine! Hop in.
          you lose the honey bread
          remember bram will row
          go to the island
        choice: Your lantern is out? Let me light it.
          Old Bram: With that little spark? Go on, then. It's on the post by the boat.
        choice: What's on the island?
          Old Bram: The Lady's shrine. She keeps the river's ember. Folk used to row out with gifts for her. Then they stopped.

  when you use the ferry lantern
    if bram will row
      say: The ferry lantern burns steady. Bram is waiting by the boat.
    otherwise
      light the ferry lantern
      say: The spark leaps from your lantern to Bram's. The wick catches with a little cough.
      Old Bram: Well, I'll be. A light on the ford again. I owe you a crossing. Talk to me when you're ready.
      remember bram will row
      add 1 to kindness

  when you look at the river
    say: Black water, moving fast. The old bridge broke in a flood before you were born, and nobody ever mended it.

  when you leave for the peak
    if you have the silver bell
      go to the peak
    otherwise
      Old Bram: Up the mountain? Nothing up there but snow, a mad old hermit, and a stone giant that never wakes.
      choose
        choice: Climb anyway.
          go to the peak
        choice: Maybe later.
          Old Bram: Wise.
